{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.MarkovGramRealSymm","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.MarkovGramRealSymm","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.LoopWeightRealSymmReduction","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.SesquilinearForm"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.MarkovGramRealSymm.tauRhoHodgeLift_of_symmForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.MarkovGramRealSymm.tauRhoHodgeLift_of_symmForm","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/MarkovGramRealSymm.lean#L72-L81","doc":"**The B2 lift from a symmetric-form loop weight.** If the loop weight is the\ncomplexified Gram of a real symmetric bilinear form, `TauRhoHodgeLift` holds — the\nreal-symmetric hypothesis discharged by the form's symmetry. STRICT: `B` here is a\n*hypothesis* (the Markov form supplies it); the τ-identification that the α_EM loop\nweight *is* this Gram remains the open categorical input, not fabricated. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.MarkovGramRealSymm.loopWeightIsRealSymm_of_symmForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.MarkovGramRealSymm.loopWeightIsRealSymm_of_symmForm","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/MarkovGramRealSymm.lean#L62-L70","doc":"**Markov-side discharge.** The complexified Gram of a real symmetric bilinear\nform satisfies the B2 premise `LoopWeightIsRealSymm`. Instantiated by the\nseminormal/Markov form (`bilinM_isSymm`), this shows the real-symmetric requirement\nis met on the Markov side — the τ-identification of the loop weight with this Gram\nis the only remaining input. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.MarkovGramRealSymm.toMatrix₂_isSymm_of_symm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.MarkovGramRealSymm.toMatrix₂_isSymm_of_symm","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/MarkovGramRealSymm.lean#L52-L60","doc":"**The Gram matrix of a symmetric ℝ-bilinear form is symmetric.** For a basis\n`b` and a bilinear form `B` with `B x y = B y x`, the matrix `toMatrix₂ b b B` is\n`IsSymm`. (Models: the seminormal / Markov-trace Gram, `bilinM_isSymm`.) ","signatureChunk":0}]}